At each stage: explain why → help complete it → review → only then advance.

## Primary user (revised)

Built for the owner's **own personal use first** — not a hypothetical generic "language learner" persona. Portfolio narrative describes this same real usage; it is not a separate audience to design for.

## Locked decisions

- **Hero**: Frictionless vocab loop — capture (0–1 taps) → vocabulary → study cards → AI.
- **Dropped**: Daily Discovery, “why today,” resurfacing archive, discovery widget, push-for-resurfacing. (**Not the same as** shuffle/random study mode — see v1 scope below.)
- **AI (offline)**: Similar words from the user's own vocabulary (duplicates allowed, no dedup) + unified search (keyword + meaning combined, one search box) — no network required.
- **AI (examples)**: Example sentences generated **on-demand** (button) for a saved word, then saved to the card; graceful fallback when unavailable — offline features still work.
- **AI (similar phrases)**: On-demand button on a card generates similar words/phrases (including idioms/collocations) beyond the user's own vocabulary, which the user can then choose to save — separate mechanism from offline similar-words, may require network.
- **Quick note widget**: Type and save a word without opening the app.
- **Resume**: Last tab only (Vocabulary vs Study) — not scroll position or mid-deck state.
- **Capture goal**: Measurably faster than Quizlet (0–1 taps from widget or Share Extension).
- **Folders**: reversed from earlier "Out" — folders are in v1 (see v1 scope). App auto-detects language on capture; every item lands in a folder — built-in per-language default folder if the user didn't pick one explicitly. User-created folders remain free-form (topic/theme/anything); manual vs automatic assignment into those is an open decision. Fallback behavior when language can't be detected is also open.

## v1 scope (locked)

In: word capture, Share Extension, vocabulary list/browse, folders (easy-access organization), unified search (keyword + meaning), similar words (own vocabulary), AI-generated similar phrases (on-demand, savable), flashcard study, shuffle/random study order, on-demand example sentences, Quick note widget, resume last tab.

Out: Daily Discovery / resurfacing feed (narrative, "why today", push), general link/photo archive, tags, markdown editor, graph view, multi-device sync, import/export, social, full language course, chat tutor, spaced repetition (v2), duplicate detection/merging.

## Your job as Tech Lead

- Protect scope. Evaluate every new idea against the hero feature first: **fast capture → vocabulary → study**.
- Do not agree with every suggestion. Push back when it doesn't serve the showcase goal.
- Do not re-introduce resurfacing / “why today” without explicit user decision.
- Advance stages only when Definition of Done is met.
- Flag scope creep, perfectionism, premature optimization, unnecessary tech.
- Leave implementation choices (frameworks, models, APIs) to **Technical Design** — not locked in product docs.
